From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] QQuickDeliveryAgent: forget the touch-mouse device when it is destroyed

While a touch point is delivered as a synthesized mouse event,
QQuickDeliveryAgentPrivate keeps the touch's device in the raw pointer
touchMouseDevice until the touch is released or cancelled. If the
device is destroyed first, for example a touchscreen unplugged or
unbound mid-touch (the evdevtouch handler deletes its QPointingDevice
when a read fails with ENODEV, and no release is ever sent), the
pointer dangles. The next press from any device then reaches
deliverPressOrReleaseEvent(), which sees isDeliveringTouchAsMouse()
still true and calls queryPointById() on the deleted device: a
use-after-free that crashes in QPointingDevicePrivate::queryPointById.

ensureDeviceConnected() already watches each device's destroyed()
signal to keep knownPointingDevices up to date; also cancel touch-mouse
synthesis there when the destroyed device is the one being synthesized
from.

Reproduced on Qt 6.11.1 (and present on dev) with a uinput touchscreen
that presses and moves over a MouseArea and is destroyed without a
release, followed by a tap from another touchscreen.

Pick-to: 6.11 6.8
---
 src/quick/util/qquickdeliveryagent.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/quick/util/qquickdeliveryagent.cpp b/src/quick/util/qquickdeliveryagent.cpp
--- a/src/quick/util/qquickdeliveryagent.cpp
+++ b/src/quick/util/qquickdeliveryagent.cpp
@@ -2017,5 +2017,9 @@ void QQuickDeliveryAgentPrivate::ensureDeviceConnected(const QPointingDevice *dev)
         return;
     knownPointingDevices.append(dev);
     connect(dev, &QPointingDevice::grabChanged, this, &QQuickDeliveryAgentPrivate::onGrabChanged);
-    QObject::connect(dev, &QObject::destroyed, q, [this, dev] {this->knownPointingDevices.removeAll(dev);});
+    QObject::connect(dev, &QObject::destroyed, q, [this, dev] {
+        knownPointingDevices.removeAll(dev);
+        if (touchMouseDevice == dev)
+            cancelTouchMouseSynthesis();
+    });
 }
